  "limitations": [
    "One active request per profile; the lane ships --max-concurrency 1 and no concurrency claim is made.",
    "Automatic checkpoints remain best effort under live traffic. Transient refusals retry up to six times per completed turn, and admission saves a session newest turn before evicting it, but a crash or an expired graceful wait can still leave unpublished work unsaved. The measured restart gate proves the two short target sessions survived, not globally loss-free shutdown.",
    "Restore and response-store capacity refusal remain possible. The lane declares a 32768 MiB host-memory floor; it was qualified on one two-GPU host and no smaller-host profile is qualified.",
    "Both native lanes share one Windows host with RTX 4090 at installation index 0 and RTX 3090 at installation index 1. The installed release binds its own GPU UUID and canonical PCI address; no GPU UUID or private host identity is included here. Only one lane may run at a time because both listen on loopback port 18082; this is not multi-GPU inference.",
    "The C1 benchmark fixture is trajectory-sensitive: its acceptance and decode rate move with changes in prefill summation order or fixture length. Measured numbers apply only to this package, this machine and this profile.",
    "The OMP phase ran the 18.0.9-hosted-windows-f4dcba581e4a client from a fresh qualification root on the target. It is not product acceptance for the unchanged stock OMP 18.8.7 client; fresh documented-route and platform acceptance remain pending.",
    "The lane pins an 11264 MiB host-KV pool with 24 host-state slots. No lane power cap is imposed; owner power is 450 W. The qualification ran with the console signed out.",
    "No rollback target exists on this two-GPU host: v0.6.10-beta.1 and earlier RTX 4090 packages are unsupported there, so the first-release rollback phase is not applicable."
  ],
